          "title": "ArtLang: Structured Language-to-Kinematics Grounding for Articulated 3D Actuation",
          "title_zh": "ArtLang：面向铰接物体三维驱动的结构化语言到运动学对齐",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.15419v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.15419",
          "summary": "ArtLang enables open-vocabulary language control of reconstructed articulated assets by representing each asset as a semantic-kinematic articulation graph and parsing commands into directive graphs with referring expressions, actions, magnitudes, reference frames, and relations. A global graph-to-graph grounding step reasons jointly about semantic, spatial, relational, and kinematic compatibility with abstention under ambiguity, and accepted directives become continuous joint targets executed through forward kinematics.",
