          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.15428",
          "summary": "The paper measures how far multiple-choice benchmark scores depend on the answer options alone, using 11,990 four-option items from a Ukrainian judicial exam; shown only the options, Claude Haiku 4.5 scores 0.383 against chance and 11.8% of items are answered blind under all eight option orders. Gating out items one model solves blind does not transfer to other models, distractor rewriting overshoots below chance, and the same probe on LEXam returns chance.",
