          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.15432",
          "summary": "The paper defines five necessary conditions for a faithful formal proof and introduces Pistis, an agentic oracle-guided proof search whose OrderDecompose strategy tracks citation dependencies and blocks unfaithful shortcuts, paired with a refutation search. Applied to the first three books of Euclid's Elements, Pistis produces compiling artifacts favored over prior work in a blinded human study and an LLM-judge protocol, and it uncovers gaps in Euclid's proofs and their translation.",
